# 6) HOSTAPD — SoftAP for WiFi provisioning (sks-hub-gecko, 2026-08-28).
#    Firmware writes /etc/hostapd.conf at runtime: open network (wpa=0),
#    driver=nl80211, ctrl_interface=/var/run/hostapd.
#    CORRECTION (2026-08-30, measured in the built rootfs): this ships THREE
#    files, not "the binary only" as first written here — Buildroot's hostapd
#    package also installs its 3383-line example /etc/hostapd.conf (ssid=test,
#    channel=1, and the same ctrl_interface=/var/run/hostapd we expect).
#    RESOLVED — the example file STAYS. sks-hub-gecko checked their side and
#    answered with the code (2026-08-30 exchange): `wifi.zig:72-76` writes the
#    conf with truncate=true at every AP entry, and `wifi.zig:271-299` orders
#    bring-up as findHostapd-or-return -> killall -> writeHostapdConf-or-return
#    -> `hostapd -B /etc/hostapd.conf`, so the only reader is reached only after
#    a successful write. With no S??hostapd at boot (measured, and as documented)
#    there is no window in which a stock `ssid=test` AP can come up. Do NOT add a
#    post-build script to delete it — that was offered and declined, because
#    deleting it would not fix the case they do care about anyway (their own
#    fallback reads this path and would then read the channel=6 they wrote).
#    They also create /var/run/hostapd themselves (`wifi.zig:144`), so the image
#    does not need to. Do not set
#    BR2_PACKAGE_HOSTAPD_WPA3 — the phone-app copy is "no password"; a
#    WPA2-only AP is an app-string change, not an image choice. nl80211
#    (default y) pulls libnl. No init script: firmware owns AP start/stop.
#    wpa_supplicant stays STA-only; CONFIG_AP is not a substitute here.
