# 4) ZIGBEE2MQTT — the hub's actual job, installed the Buildroot way rather than as a
#    hand-staged /opt tree. package/nodejs/nodejs.mk already wires npm for cross builds
#    (NODEJS_BIN_ENV: npm_config_arch/target_arch=arm64, build_from_source=true,
#    npm_config_nodedir=$(STAGING_DIR)/usr, npm_config_prefix=$(TARGET_DIR)/usr), and
#    nodejs-src.mk runs `npm install -g <list>` from INSTALL_TARGET_CMDS. So
#    @serialport/bindings-cpp is compiled against our aarch64 sysroot with node-gyp
#    instead of resolving an x86_64 prebuild, and the tree lands in
#    /usr/lib/node_modules/zigbee2mqtt — the "bake Node/ICU/Z2M into rootfs /usr"
#    decision from 2026-07-22, not SMHub's /opt + opkg shape.
#
#    PINNED, not floating. Buildroot's help text says "for repeatable builds, download
#    and save tgz files"; an unpinned name would resolve to whatever npm serves that day
#    and the image would stop being reproducible. 2.10.1 is the SMHub reference product's
#    version (opkg zigbee2mqtt 2.10.1-2 → zigbee-herdsman 10.0.7, converters 26.46.0,
#    frontend 0.9.21) and its engines field is "^20.15.0 || ^22.2.0 || ^24", satisfied by
#    the Node 22.22.0 above — which is also the exact Node SMHub ships.
BR2_PACKAGE_NODEJS_MODULES_ADDITIONAL="zigbee2mqtt@2.10.1"

# 5) MQTT BROKER — Z2M is a bridge, not a broker; it needs one to publish to. Local
#    mosquitto keeps the hub self-contained (no external broker to configure at first
#    boot). Buildroot ships an S50mosquitto init script, which orders ahead of the
#    S70zigbee2mqtt in bsp/overlay/common.
BR2_PACKAGE_MOSQUITTO=y
